# Geograph CLIP Processor (including ClipTheLandscape)
===

Docker Port of 
https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1yArUW04Q-wZAoEiv6SsjWuf3K0d7yx-c

* This contains a client processor script, it computes the CLIP encodings for batches of Geograph images, and 
submits them to a central repository. The server provides URLs to presized 224x224px images, the client 
handles running them though CLIP preprocess/tokenize and the encoding step of the image and title.

* This allows the processing to be distributed over many 'clients', so we don't have to compute these 
encodings ourselves.

* At the same time also runs one of ClipTheLandscape models to infer Context Tags, this is just side project 
as computing the predicted context tags is an experiment to test the model at scale. (as have the CLIP 
encodings very quick to run them though one of the models)

For background on the ClipTheLandscape project, see
https://github.com/SpaceTimeLab/ClipTheLandscape/


Gemini was used extensively to create this Docker Image
https://gemini.google.com/app/8266f4fb4876dd25

    sudo docker build -t clip-processor .


* The final image is published: https://hub.docker.com/r/geograph/clip-processor that container will run one 
invokation of this script, also 100 loops.

More information on running the client: 
   https://staging.data.geograph.org.uk/facets/clipprocessor.html

